10 REM THE NEXT LEAD OF AN IDENTIFICATION KEY, ONE QUESTION AT A TIME:
12 REM ANSWER 1 YES TAKES THE YES LEAD, 0 NO THE NO LEAD, -1 NOT SURE
14 REM GIVES 0, SINCE THE KEY NEVER GUESSES. A LEAD IS A COUPLET (ABOVE
16 REM 0), A TAXON REACHED (NEGATED) OR 0. AN ANSWER OUTSIDE -1..1 OR A
18 REM LEAD PAST 999999999 EITHER WAY IS REFUSED.
20 INPUT A, Y, N
30 IF A < -1 THEN 300
40 IF A > 1 THEN 300
50 IF Y < -999999999 THEN 300
60 IF Y > 999999999 THEN 300
70 IF N < -999999999 THEN 300
80 IF N > 999999999 THEN 300
90 LET L = 0
100 IF A = 1 THEN 130
110 IF A = 0 THEN 150
120 GOTO 200
130 LET L = Y
140 GOTO 200
150 LET L = N
200 PRINT L
210 GOTO 310
300 PRINT "REFUSED"
310 END
